    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "**Interpreting these plots:** in each pair, the left panel shows one horizontal \"silhouette blade\" per cluster — a wide, uniformly long blade that mostly stays to the right of the red dashed average line means that cluster's points are tightly and confidently grouped. A thin, short, or negative blade means that cluster is weak or poorly separated. The right panel shows the same clustering laid over our PCA plot, so you can visually confirm what the silhouette blades are telling you numerically. When we get to `k=4` (matching our true number of groups), you should see 4 fairly healthy, similarly-sized blades — good visual confirmation that 4 is indeed the right choice, arrived at without ever consulting the answer key.\n",
