      "source": [
        "**Interpreting this:** `cv=5` means the training data gets split into 5 chunks; the model trains on 4 of them and checks itself against the 5th, rotating through all 5 combinations, and averages the results. This lets the computer estimate, honestly, which value of `C` (from our candidate list) generalizes best — without ever peeking at the true test set while making that choice. The **test accuracy** printed last is the number that actually matters for judging real-world performance, since it's evaluated on wines the whole process never touched during training or tuning.\n",
