        "\n",
        "- **A plain scatter plot of high-dimensional data is almost always misleading** — it's showing you 2 out of possibly hundreds of measurements, essentially at random.\n",
        "- **PCA, MDS, and t-SNE each answer a different question**: PCA maximizes spread, MDS preserves overall distances, t-SNE preserves local neighborhoods. They can (and often do) produce visually different-looking plots of the exact same data — that's not a bug, it's a reflection of what each method is actually optimizing for.\n",
        "- **K-means needs you to choose the number of clusters**, but statistical diagnostics — the elbow method, the silhouette score, and the more detailed Yellowbrick silhouette visualizer — can recover the correct number even without ever seeing the true labels.\n",
