        "- On real wine chemistry data, **unsupervised clustering (blind to labels) successfully rediscovered the 3 true grape varieties**, and a supervised classifier trained on just 2 well-chosen chemical measurements performed nearly as well as one trained on all 13.\n",
        "- **Always evaluate a classifier on data it never saw during training or tuning** — that's the only honest measure of how it will perform on genuinely new samples."
